<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <ctb-tab-group class="flex flex-col gap-4 w-full">
        <ctb-segmented-control>
            <button type="button" selected>Errors</button>
            <button type="button">Incorrect Answers</button>
        </ctb-segmented-control>

        <ctb-layout id="pane-help-errors" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <h3>Errors Explanation</h3>
            <p>If you encounter an unexpected error during arithmetic evaluation, division by zero, or integer overflow:</p>
            <p><strong>What To Do:</strong> Click 'Clear All' or restart the calculation and verify operand bounds.</p>
        </ctb-layout>

        <ctb-layout id="pane-help-incorrect" class="flex flex-col gap-2" hidden>
            <h3>Frequently Asked Questions &amp; Troubleshooting</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Modulo vs Integer Division:</strong> <code>\</code> returns the integer quotient without fractional parts, while <code>Mod</code> returns the remainder.</li>
                <li><strong>Floating-point Precision:</strong> Values are computed using standard IEEE-754 64-bit precision.</li>
                <li><strong>Complex Square Roots:</strong> When evaluating negative numbers in Square Root mode, the output displays an imaginary suffix <code>i</code>.</li>
            </ul>
        </ctb-layout>
    </ctb-tab-group>
</div>
